# {{ .ServiceTitle }}

Generated with `hyperserve-init`. This project starts with ordinary HTTP
handlers, browser security headers, route-scoped rate limiting, health checks,
and optional MCP transport.

## Quick Start

```bash
go run ./cmd/server
```

The server listens on `{{ .DefaultAddr }}` by default and exposes a health server on `{{ .DefaultHealthAddr }}`.

## Configuration

Configuration lives in `configs/default.json`. Override any value with environment variables:

- `HS_MCP_ENABLED=true` enables Model Context Protocol support.
- `SERVER_ADDR=":9090"` changes the HTTP listener.

`HeadersMiddleware` applies browser security headers to every application
route. HyperServe omits its `Server` identification header by default.

MCP is disabled unless the project was generated with `--with-mcp` or enabled
later through configuration. The generated endpoint starts without built-in
tools or resources because the generator cannot choose an authorization
policy. Protect `/mcp` before registering application capabilities.

## Deployment

- `make build` produces a hardened binary.
- `make docker-build` builds the container image defined in `Dockerfile`.

